roblem\": \"Long-lived secrets checked into config or baked into images\",\n   \"owner\": \"B03\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"problem\": \"Incoming hostile payloads not validated\",\n   \"owner\": \"R01\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"problem\": \"Retrieval returning another tenant's documents\",\n   \"owner\": \"R04\"\n  }\n ],\n \"na_when\": \"never\",\n \"checks\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"R03.1\",\n   \"check\": \"Secrets and sensitive fields are redacted from tool output, debug output, and error text before they reach the model, outside recipients, or normal logs.\",\n   \"coverage_required\": true,\n   \"verify\": \"1) Find redaction code (`redact`, `mask`, secret patterns) and where tool output, errors, and debug text go. 2) Check redaction runs before the model, outside recipients, and logs. 3) Answer no if any path skips it, such as error messages, exception traces, debug logging, or `logger.info(response)` before redaction.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"R03.2\",\n   \"check\": \"The display client blocks auto-fetched URLs (Markdown images, link previews) or allows only approved hosts.\",\n   \"coverage_required\": true,\n   \"verify\": \"1) Find the display client or renderer (Markdown render, link unfurl, image tags). 2) Check auto-fetched URLs are blocked or limited to approved hosts (CSP `img-src`, URL allowlist). 3) Answer no if Markdown images or previews load any URL. Answer unknown if the display client is outside this repo.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"R03.3\",\n   \"check\": \"Generated SQL uses parameterized queries, shell calls use argument lists with no string-built commands, and HTML output is escaped for its context.\",\n   \"coverage_required\": true,\n   \"verify\": \"1) Search for SQL, shell, and HTML built from generated output (`execute(f`, `+ query`, `shell=True`, `exec(`, `innerHTML`, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, `|safe`). 2) Check for parameters, argument lists, and context escaping. 3) Answer no if any query or command is string-built, uses `shell=True` or `sh -c` with model input, or HTML is unescaped.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"R03.4\",\n   \"check\": \"Redacted audit evidence is kept rather than discarded.\",\n   \"coverage_required\": true,\n   \"verify\": \"1) Find redaction code and audit logging. 2) Check redacted records are written to an audit store. 3) Answer no if redaction drops the whole record, or the evidence is discarded instead of kept.\"\n  }\n ]\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019BqLmw1ij7gnqfM5aDRPJP","type":"tool_result","content":"# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7\nFROM node:22.11-bookworm-slim@sha256:3f1a8d2c9b7e4f6a5d0c8b1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a AS build\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY package.json package-lock.json ./\nRUN npm ci --ignore-scripts\nCOPY tsconfig.json ./\nCOPY src ./src\nRUN npm run build && npm prune --omit=dev\n\nFROM gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian12:nonroot@sha256:9b2e4c6a8d0f1e3c5a7b9d1f3e5c7a9b1d3f5e7c9a1b3d5f7e9c1a3b5d7f9e1c\nWORKDIR /app\nENV NODE_ENV=production \\\n    CLINIC_AGENT_ROOT=/app\nCOPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/node_modules ./node_modules\nCOPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/dist ./dist\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 package.json ./\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 prompts ./prompts\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 config ./config\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 release ./release\nUSER 65532:65532\nEXPOSE 8080\nCMD [\"dist/server.js\"]\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Namespace\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent\n  labels:\n    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted\n    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version: v1.33\n    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit: restricted\n    pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn: restricted\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ServiceAccount\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent\n  namespace: clinic-agent\n  annotations:\n    eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\n    eks.amazonaws.com/token-expiration: \"3600\"\nautomountServiceAccountToken: false\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ServiceAccount\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent-reminders\n  namespace: clinic-agent\n  annotations:\n    eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\nautomountServiceAccountToken: false\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent\n  namespace: clinic-agent\ndata:\n  CLINIC_DIRECTORY: |\n    [{\"id\":\"nb-castro\",\"name\":\"Northbay Castro\",\"smsNumber\":\"+14155550110\"},\n     {\"id\":\"nb-fremont\",\"name\":\"Northbay Fremont\",\"smsNumber\":\"+15105550111\"},\n     {\"id\":\"nb-oakland\",\"name\":\"Northbay Oakland\",\"smsNumber\":\"+15105550112\"},\n     {\"id\":\"nb-sanmateo\",\"name\":\"Northbay San Mateo\",\"smsNumber\":\"+16505550113\"},\n     {\"id\":\"nb-walnutcreek\",\"name\":\"Northbay Walnut Creek\",\"smsNumber\":\"+19255550114\"}]\n  SMS_SIGNING_SECRET_ARN: arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-west-2:418295730611:secret:clinic-agent/sms-signing\n  HTTPS_PROXY: http://egress-proxy.platform.svc.cluster.local:3128\n  NO_PROXY: ehr-mcp.internal.northbay-clinics.example,.svc.cluster.local\n---\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent\n  namespace: clinic-agent\n  labels: { app: clinic-agent }\nspec:\n  replicas: 3\n  selector:\n    matchLabels: { app: clinic-agent }\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels: { app: clinic-agent }\n    spec:\n      serviceAccountName: clinic-agent\n      automountServiceAccountToken: false\n      hostUsers: false\n      hostNetwork: false\n      hostPID: false\n      hostIPC: false\n      enableServiceLinks: false\n      securityContext:\n        runAsNonRoot: true\n        runAsUser: 65532\n        runAsGroup: 65532\n        fsGroup: 65532\n        seccompProfile:\n          type: RuntimeDefault\n      containers:\n        - name: agent\n          image: 418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n          ports:\n            - containerPort: 8080\n          envFrom:\n            - configMapRef: { name: clinic-agent }\n          env:\n            - name: IMAGE_DIGEST\n              value: sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n            - name: GIT_SHA\n              value: e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\n          securityContext:\n            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n            privileged: false\n            readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n            runAsNonRoot: true\n            capabilities:\n              drop: [\"ALL\"]\n            seccompProfile:\n              type: RuntimeDefault\n          resources:\n            requests: { cpu: 250m, memory: 384Mi }\n            limits: { cpu: \"1\", memory: 768Mi }\n          readinessProbe:\n            httpGet: { path: /healthz, port: 8080 }\n          volumeMounts:\n            - { name: tmp, mountPath: /tmp }\n            - { name: sts-token, mountPath: /var/run/secrets/tokens, readOnly: true }\n      volumes:\n        - name: tmp\n          emptyDir: { medium: Memory, sizeLimit: 32Mi }\n        - name: sts-token\n          projected:\n            sources:\n              - serviceAccountToken:\n                  audience: https://sts.northbay-clinics.example\n                  expirationSeconds: 900\n                  path: sts-token\n---\napiVersion: batch/v1\nkind: CronJob\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent-reminders\n  namespace: clinic-agent\nspec:\n  schedule: \"0 17 * * *\"\n  timeZone: America/Los_Angeles\n  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid\n  jobTemplate:\n    spec:\n      backoffLimit: 0\n      activeDeadlineSeconds: 1800\n      template:\n        metadata:\n          labels: { app: clinic-agent-reminders }\n        spec:\n          serviceAccountName: clinic-agent-reminders\n          automountServiceAccountToken: false\n          restartPolicy: Never\n          hostUsers: false\n          securityContext:\n            runAsNonRoot: true\n            runAsUser: 65532\n            runAsGroup: 65532\n            seccompProfile:\n              type: RuntimeDefault\n          containers:\n            - name: reminders\n              image: 418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n              args: [\"dist/workers/reminders.js\"]\n              envFrom:\n                - configMapRef: { name: clinic-agent }\n              env:\n                - name: IMAGE_DIGEST\n                  value: sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n                - name: GIT_SHA\n                  value: e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\n              securityContext:\n                allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n                privileged: false\n                readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n                capabilities:\n                  drop: [\"ALL\"]\n---\n# Egress: DNS, the EHR MCP endpoint (private link), and the platform egress proxy only.\n# The proxy allows api.anthropic.com, the payments and SMS providers, the eligibility agent,\n# the group STS and auth service, and AWS service endpoints.\napiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: NetworkPolicy\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent-egress\n  namespace: clinic-agent\nspec:\n  podSelector: {}\n  policyTypes: [\"Egress\", \"Ingress\"]\n  ingress:\n    - from:\n        - namespaceSelector:\n            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: ingress }\n      ports:\n        - { port: 8080, protocol: TCP }\n  egress:\n    - to:\n        - namespaceSelector:\n            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: kube-system }\n          podSelector:\n            matchLabels: { k8s-app: kube-dns }\n      ports:\n        - { port: 53, protocol: UDP }\n        - { port: 53, protocol: TCP }\n    - to:\n        - namespaceSelector:\n            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: platform }\n          podSelector:\n            matchLabels: { app: egress-proxy }\n      ports:\n        - { port: 3128, protocol: TCP }\n    - to:\n        - ipBlock: { cidr: 10.60.12.0/28 }\n      ports:\n        - { port: 443, protocol: TCP }\n# Security-relevant paths need a review from the platform leads in addition to the two\n# approvals required by branch protection (infra/terraform/github.tf).\n*                    @northbay-clinics/clinic-agent-devs\n/prompts/            @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\n/config/             @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\n/release/            @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\n/infra/              @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads @northbay-clinics/cloud-security\n/k8s/                @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads @northbay-clinics/cloud-security\n/.github/            @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads @northbay-clinics/cloud-security\n/src/tools/          @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\n/src/control/        @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\n/src/audit/          @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\nname: ci\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@08eba0b27e820071cde6df949e0beb9ba4906955 # v4.3.0\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@a0853c24544627f65ddf259abe73b1d18a591444 # v5.0.0\n        with:\n          node-version: \"22.11\"\n          cache: npm\n      - run: npm ci --ignore-scripts\n      - run: npm run lint\n      - run: npm test\n      - run: npm run build\n\n  manifest-check:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@08eba0b27e820071cde6df949e0beb9ba4906955 # v4.3.0\n      - name: Prompt digests match the release manifest\n        run: |\n          node -e '\n            const fs = require(\"fs\"), crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n            const m = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\"release/manifest.json\", \"utf8\"));\n            let bad = 0;\n            for (const p of m.prompts) {\n              const got = crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(p.path)).digest(\"hex\");\n              if (got !== p.sha256) { console.error(`${p.path}: manifest ${p.sha256} != file ${got}`); bad++; }\n            }\n            const ver = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\"package.json\", \"utf8\")).version;\n            if (m.harness.version !== ver) { console.error(`harness version ${m.harness.version} != package ${ver}`); bad++; }\n            process.exit(bad ? 1 : 0);\n          '\n\n  image:\n    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'\n    needs: [test, manifest-check]\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      id-token: write\n      attestations: write\n      packages: write\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@08eba0b27e820071cde6df949e0beb9ba4906955 # v4.3.0\n      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@a03048d87541d1d9fcf2ecf528a4a65ba9bd7838 # v5.0.0\n        with:\n          role-to-assume: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-image-build\n          aws-region: us-west-2\n      - uses: aws-actions/amazon-ecr-login@062b18b96a7aff071d4dc91bc00c4c1a7945b076 # v2.0.1\n        id: ecr\n      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@e468171a9de216ec08956ac3ada2f0791b6bd435 # v3.11.1\n      - uses: docker/build-push-action@263435318d21b8e681c14492fe198d362a7d2c83 # v6.18.0\n        id: build\n        with:\n          push: true\n          tags: ${{ steps.ecr.outputs.registry }}/clinic-agent:${{ github.sha }}\n          provenance: mode=max\n          sbom: true\n      - uses: sigstore/cosign-installer@d58896d6a1865668819e1d91763c7751a165e159 # v3.9.2\n        with:\n          cosign-release: v2.6.2\n      - name: Sign image\n        run: cosign sign --yes ${{ steps.ecr.outputs.registry }}/clinic-agent@${{ steps.build.outputs.digest }}\n      - uses: actions/attest-build-provenance@977bb373ede98d70efdf65b84cb5f73e068dcc2a # v3.0.0\n        with:\n          subject-name: ${{ steps.ecr.outputs.registry }}/clinic-agent\n          subject-digest: ${{ steps.build.outputs.digest }}\n          push-to-registry: true\nname: deploy\n\n# Deploys the image digest named in release/manifest.json. The digest reaches the manifest through\n# a reviewed release PR, so what runs is always a reviewed commit.\non:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      emergency:\n        description: Emergency change (hotfix/* branch, production-emergency environment)\n        type: boolean\n        default: false\n      owner:\n        description: Emergency only - person accountable for this change\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n      reason:\n        description: Emergency only - why this cannot wait for a normal release\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n      expires_on:\n        description: Emergency only - date (YYYY-MM-DD) by which it is replaced by a normal release\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n  id-token: write\n  issues: write\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: deploy-production\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    environment: ${{ inputs.emergency && 'production-emergency' || 'production' }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@08eba0b27e820071cde6df949e0beb9ba4906955 # v4.3.0\n\n      - name: Emergency change record is complete\n        if: inputs.emergency\n        env:\n          OWNER: ${{ inputs.owner }}\n          REASON: ${{ inputs.reason }}\n          EXPIRES_ON: ${{ inputs.expires_on }}\n        run: |\n          test -n \"$OWNER\" || { echo \"owner is required\"; exit 1; }\n          test -n \"$REASON\" || { echo \"reason is required\"; exit 1; }\n          date -d \"$EXPIRES_ON\" +%F >/dev/null || { echo \"expires_on must be a date\"; exit 1; }\n          [[ \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" == hotfix/* ]] || { echo \"emergency deploys come from hotfix/* branches\"; exit 1; }\n\n      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@a03048d87541d1d9fcf2ecf528a4a65ba9bd7838 # v5.0.0\n        with:\n          role-to-assume: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-deploy\n          aws-region: us-west-2\n\n      - uses: sigstore/cosign-installer@d58896d6a1865668819e1d91763c7751a165e159 # v3.9.2\n        with:\n          cosign-release: v2.6.2\n\n      - name: Verify image signature\n        run: |\n          DIGEST=$(jq -r .image.digest release/manifest.json)\n          REPO=$(jq -r .image.repository release/manifest.json)\n          cosign verify \"$REPO@$DIGEST\" \\\n            --certificate-identity \"https://github.com/northbay-clinics/clinic-agent/.github/workflows/ci.yml@refs/heads/main\" \\\n            --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\n          grep -q \"$DIGEST\" k8s/deployment.yaml || { echo \"k8s/deployment.yaml does not use the manifest digest\"; exit 1; }\n\n      - name: Apply\n        run: |\n          aws eks update-kubeconfig --name clinic-agent-prod\n          kubectl apply -f k8s/deployment.yaml\n          kubectl -n clinic-agent annotate deployment/clinic-agent --overwrite \\\n            northbay.example/git-sha=\"$GITHUB_SHA\" \\\n            northbay.example/release=\"$(jq -r .release release/manifest.json)\" \\\n            northbay.example/deployed-by=\"$GITHUB_ACTOR\" \\\n            northbay.example/run=\"$GITHUB_SERVER_URL/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$GITHUB_RUN_ID\"\n          kubectl -n clinic-agent rollout status deployment/clinic-agent --timeout=5m\n\n      - name: Open follow-up review for emergency change\n        if: inputs.emergency\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          OWNER: ${{ inputs.owner }}\n          REASON: ${{ inputs.reason }}\n          EXPIRES_ON: ${{ inputs.expires_on }}\n        run: |\n          gh issue create \\\n            --title \"Follow-up review: emergency deploy ${GITHUB_SHA::8}\" \\\n            --label emergency-change,needs-review \\\n            --assignee \"$OWNER\" \\\n            --body \"Owner: $OWNER\n          Reason: $REASON\n          Ends: $EXPIRES_ON\n          Commit: $GITHUB_SHA\n          Approved in environment production-emergency by a required reviewer (see run $GITHUB_RUN_ID).\n          Review and merge to main via normal PR before the end date.\"\n{\n  \"release\": \"clinic-agent-3.4.1\",\n  \"agentTypeId\": \"sha256:7c2e91f04ab35d6e8f1029c4b7a6d3e5f8091a2b3c4d5e6f708192a3b4c5d6e7\",\n  \"image\": {\n    \"repository\": \"418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent\",\n    \"digest\": \"sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\"\n  },\n  \"harness\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.4.1\",\n    \"gitSha\": \"e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\"\n  },\n  \"prompts\": [\n    { \"path\": \"prompts/system.md\", \"sha256\": \"5d1e0c9b8a7f6e5d4c3b2a1908f7e6d5c4b3a291807f6e5d4c3b2a19087f6e5d\" },\n    { \"path\": \"prompts/intent-classifier.txt\", \"sha256\": \"a3f9e1d7c5b3a1f9e7d5c3b1a9f7e5d3c1b9a7f5e3d1c9b7a5f3e1d9c7b5a3f1\" }\n  ],\n  \"models\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"agent\",\n      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n      \"requestedId\": \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\n      \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n      \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n      \"adapter\": null,\n      \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"intent_classifier\",\n      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n      \"requestedId\": \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\",\n      \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n      \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n      \"adapter\": null,\n      \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": {\n    \"allowlist\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\",\n    \"mcpServers\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"ehr\",\n        \"url\": \"https://ehr-mcp.internal.northbay-clinics.example/mcp\",\n        \"tlsCertSha256\": \"1f6a9c3e5b7d9f1a3c5e7b9d1f3a5c7e9b1d3f5a7c9e1b3d5f7a9c1e3b5d7f9a\",\n        \"owner\": \"ehr-integrations@northbay-clinics.example\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"native\": [\"payments\", \"sms\", \"insurance\"]\n  },\n  \"peers\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"eligibility-agent\",\n      \"url\": \"https://eligibility.partners.northbay-clinics.example/a2a\",\n      \"owner\": \"revenue-cycle@northbay-clinics.example\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"awsRole\": \"arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\",\n    \"ehrScopes\": [\"patient.read\", \"appointment.read\", \"appointment.write\"],\n    \"paymentsScopes\": [\"deposits.refund\"],\n    \"eligibilityScopes\": [\"eligibility:read\"]\n  },\n  \"memory\": \"none\",\n  \"retrieval\": \"none\",\n  \"network\": { \"policy\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml#clinic-agent-egress\", \"egressProxy\": \"egress-proxy.platform.svc:3128\" },\n  \"budgets\": \"config/budgets.yaml\",\n  \"policies\": { \"action\": \"config/policy.yaml\", \"actionPolicyVersion\": \"2026-09-18.3\" }\n}\n# clinic-agent\n\nPatient-scheduling agent for the Northbay Clinic Group. Patients reach it by SMS or by the web chat\nwidget on each clinic's site. It looks up, books, reschedules, and cancels appointments in the EHR,\nsends SMS reminders, refunds no-show deposits, and asks the insurance-eligibility agent whether a\nvisit is covered.\n\nEach clinic is a tenant. A clinic's patients, appointments, deposits, and EHR credentials are kept\nseparate from every other clinic's.\n\n## Components\n\n| Piece | Where | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n\nThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\nthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n\n## High-impact actions\n\n`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\nthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\nretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n\n```bash\naws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\\n  --item '{\"pk\":{\"S\":\"global\"},\"halted\":{\"BOOL\":true},\"by\":{\"S\":\"<you>\"}}'\n```\n\nRunning work checks the flag before each model turn and each tool call, and a watcher aborts in-flight\nrequests within 2 seconds.\n\n## Identity\n\n`src/agent/identity.ts` computes the agent-type-id from the image digest, harness version, prompts,\nmodel IDs, and config. Each pod also gets a random agent-instance-id at start. Both are on every\naudit record together with the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, and trace context.\n\n## Build and test\n\n```bash\nnpm ci\nnpm run lint\nnpm test\nnpm run build\n```\n\n## Release\n\nMerges to `main` need two reviews and a code owner review for prompts, config, infra, and manifests.\n`deploy.yml` builds, signs, and deploys by digest to the `production` environment, which has required\nreviewers. Emergency deploys use the same workflow with `emergency: true` and must name an owner,\na reason, and an end date; the workflow opens a follow-up review issue.\n\n## Owners\n\n- Accountable party: Northbay Clinic Group, Patient Access (VP Patient Access)\n- Operational owner: agent-platform team, `#agent-platform-oncall`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f536b84-c330-4aae-a36d-08180bd73505","uuid":"3792ed33-d457-495c-bdb4-d838b2294055","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:03:33.564Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7\nFROM node:22.11-bookworm-slim@sha256:3f1a8d2c9b7e4f6a5d0c8b1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a AS build\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY package.json package-lock.json ./\nRUN npm ci --ignore-scripts\nCOPY tsconfig.json ./\nCOPY src ./src\nRUN npm run build && npm prune --omit=dev\n\nFROM gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian12:nonroot@sha256:9b2e4c6a8d0f1e3c5a7b9d1f3e5c7a9b1d3f5e7c9a1b3d5f7e9c1a3b5d7f9e1c\nWORKDIR /app\nENV NODE_ENV=production \\\n    CLINIC_AGENT_ROOT=/app\nCOPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/node_modules ./node_modules\nCOPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/dist ./dist\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 package.json ./\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 prompts ./prompts\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 config ./config\nCOPY --chown=65532:65532 release ./release\nUSER 65532:65532\nEXPOSE 8080\nCMD [\"dist/server.js\"]\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Namespace\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent\n  labels:\n    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted\n    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version: v1.33\n    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit: restricted\n    pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn: restricted\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ServiceAccount\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent\n  namespace: clinic-agent\n  annotations:\n    eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\n    eks.amazonaws.com/token-expiration: \"3600\"\nautomountServiceAccountToken: false\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ServiceAccount\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent-reminders\n  namespace: clinic-agent\n  annotations:\n    eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\nautomountServiceAccountToken: false\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent\n  namespace: clinic-agent\ndata:\n  CLINIC_DIRECTORY: |\n    [{\"id\":\"nb-castro\",\"name\":\"Northbay Castro\",\"smsNumber\":\"+14155550110\"},\n     {\"id\":\"nb-fremont\",\"name\":\"Northbay Fremont\",\"smsNumber\":\"+15105550111\"},\n     {\"id\":\"nb-oakland\",\"name\":\"Northbay Oakland\",\"smsNumber\":\"+15105550112\"},\n     {\"id\":\"nb-sanmateo\",\"name\":\"Northbay San Mateo\",\"smsNumber\":\"+16505550113\"},\n     {\"id\":\"nb-walnutcreek\",\"name\":\"Northbay Walnut Creek\",\"smsNumber\":\"+19255550114\"}]\n  SMS_SIGNING_SECRET_ARN: arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-west-2:418295730611:secret:clinic-agent/sms-signing\n  HTTPS_PROXY: http://egress-proxy.platform.svc.cluster.local:3128\n  NO_PROXY: ehr-mcp.internal.northbay-clinics.example,.svc.cluster.local\n---\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent\n  namespace: clinic-agent\n  labels: { app: clinic-agent }\nspec:\n  replicas: 3\n  selector:\n    matchLabels: { app: clinic-agent }\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels: { app: clinic-agent }\n    spec:\n      serviceAccountName: clinic-agent\n      automountServiceAccountToken: false\n      hostUsers: false\n      hostNetwork: false\n      hostPID: false\n      hostIPC: false\n      enableServiceLinks: false\n      securityContext:\n        runAsNonRoot: true\n        runAsUser: 65532\n        runAsGroup: 65532\n        fsGroup: 65532\n        seccompProfile:\n          type: RuntimeDefault\n      containers:\n        - name: agent\n          image: 418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n          ports:\n            - containerPort: 8080\n          envFrom:\n            - configMapRef: { name: clinic-agent }\n          env:\n            - name: IMAGE_DIGEST\n              value: sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n            - name: GIT_SHA\n              value: e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\n          securityContext:\n            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n            privileged: false\n            readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n            runAsNonRoot: true\n            capabilities:\n              drop: [\"ALL\"]\n            seccompProfile:\n              type: RuntimeDefault\n          resources:\n            requests: { cpu: 250m, memory: 384Mi }\n            limits: { cpu: \"1\", memory: 768Mi }\n          readinessProbe:\n            httpGet: { path: /healthz, port: 8080 }\n          volumeMounts:\n            - { name: tmp, mountPath: /tmp }\n            - { name: sts-token, mountPath: /var/run/secrets/tokens, readOnly: true }\n      volumes:\n        - name: tmp\n          emptyDir: { medium: Memory, sizeLimit: 32Mi }\n        - name: sts-token\n          projected:\n            sources:\n              - serviceAccountToken:\n                  audience: https://sts.northbay-clinics.example\n                  expirationSeconds: 900\n                  path: sts-token\n---\napiVersion: batch/v1\nkind: CronJob\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent-reminders\n  namespace: clinic-agent\nspec:\n  schedule: \"0 17 * * *\"\n  timeZone: America/Los_Angeles\n  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid\n  jobTemplate:\n    spec:\n      backoffLimit: 0\n      activeDeadlineSeconds: 1800\n      template:\n        metadata:\n          labels: { app: clinic-agent-reminders }\n        spec:\n          serviceAccountName: clinic-agent-reminders\n          automountServiceAccountToken: false\n          restartPolicy: Never\n          hostUsers: false\n          securityContext:\n            runAsNonRoot: true\n            runAsUser: 65532\n            runAsGroup: 65532\n            seccompProfile:\n              type: RuntimeDefault\n          containers:\n            - name: reminders\n              image: 418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n              args: [\"dist/workers/reminders.js\"]\n              envFrom:\n                - configMapRef: { name: clinic-agent }\n              env:\n                - name: IMAGE_DIGEST\n                  value: sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n                - name: GIT_SHA\n                  value: e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\n              securityContext:\n                allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n                privileged: false\n                readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n                capabilities:\n                  drop: [\"ALL\"]\n---\n# Egress: DNS, the EHR MCP endpoint (private link), and the platform egress proxy only.\n# The proxy allows api.anthropic.com, the payments and SMS providers, the eligibility agent,\n# the group STS and auth service, and AWS service endpoints.\napiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: NetworkPolicy\nmetadata:\n  name: clinic-agent-egress\n  namespace: clinic-agent\nspec:\n  podSelector: {}\n  policyTypes: [\"Egress\", \"Ingress\"]\n  ingress:\n    - from:\n        - namespaceSelector:\n            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: ingress }\n      ports:\n        - { port: 8080, protocol: TCP }\n  egress:\n    - to:\n        - namespaceSelector:\n            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: kube-system }\n          podSelector:\n            matchLabels: { k8s-app: kube-dns }\n      ports:\n        - { port: 53, protocol: UDP }\n        - { port: 53, protocol: TCP }\n    - to:\n        - namespaceSelector:\n            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: platform }\n          podSelector:\n            matchLabels: { app: egress-proxy }\n      ports:\n        - { port: 3128, protocol: TCP }\n    - to:\n        - ipBlock: { cidr: 10.60.12.0/28 }\n      ports:\n        - { port: 443, protocol: TCP }\n# Security-relevant paths need a review from the platform leads in addition to the two\n# approvals required by branch protection (infra/terraform/github.tf).\n*                    @northbay-clinics/clinic-agent-devs\n/prompts/            @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\n/config/             @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\n/release/            @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\n/infra/              @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads @northbay-clinics/cloud-security\n/k8s/                @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads @northbay-clinics/cloud-security\n/.github/            @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads @northbay-clinics/cloud-security\n/src/tools/          @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\n/src/control/        @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\n/src/audit/          @northbay-clinics/agent-platform-leads\nname: ci\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@08eba0b27e820071cde6df949e0beb9ba4906955 # v4.3.0\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@a0853c24544627f65ddf259abe73b1d18a591444 # v5.0.0\n        with:\n          node-version: \"22.11\"\n          cache: npm\n      - run: npm ci --ignore-scripts\n      - run: npm run lint\n      - run: npm test\n      - run: npm run build\n\n  manifest-check:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@08eba0b27e820071cde6df949e0beb9ba4906955 # v4.3.0\n      - name: Prompt digests match the release manifest\n        run: |\n          node -e '\n            const fs = require(\"fs\"), crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n            const m = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\"release/manifest.json\", \"utf8\"));\n            let bad = 0;\n            for (const p of m.prompts) {\n              const got = crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(p.path)).digest(\"hex\");\n              if (got !== p.sha256) { console.error(`${p.path}: manifest ${p.sha256} != file ${got}`); bad++; }\n            }\n            const ver = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\"package.json\", \"utf8\")).version;\n            if (m.harness.version !== ver) { console.error(`harness version ${m.harness.version} != package ${ver}`); bad++; }\n            process.exit(bad ? 1 : 0);\n          '\n\n  image:\n    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'\n    needs: [test, manifest-check]\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      id-token: write\n      attestations: write\n      packages: write\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@08eba0b27e820071cde6df949e0beb9ba4906955 # v4.3.0\n      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@a03048d87541d1d9fcf2ecf528a4a65ba9bd7838 # v5.0.0\n        with:\n          role-to-assume: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-image-build\n          aws-region: us-west-2\n      - uses: aws-actions/amazon-ecr-login@062b18b96a7aff071d4dc91bc00c4c1a7945b076 # v2.0.1\n        id: ecr\n      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@e468171a9de216ec08956ac3ada2f0791b6bd435 # v3.11.1\n      - uses: docker/build-push-action@263435318d21b8e681c14492fe198d362a7d2c83 # v6.18.0\n        id: build\n        with:\n          push: true\n          tags: ${{ steps.ecr.outputs.registry }}/clinic-agent:${{ github.sha }}\n          provenance: mode=max\n          sbom: true\n      - uses: sigstore/cosign-installer@d58896d6a1865668819e1d91763c7751a165e159 # v3.9.2\n        with:\n          cosign-release: v2.6.2\n      - name: Sign image\n        run: cosign sign --yes ${{ steps.ecr.outputs.registry }}/clinic-agent@${{ steps.build.outputs.digest }}\n      - uses: actions/attest-build-provenance@977bb373ede98d70efdf65b84cb5f73e068dcc2a # v3.0.0\n        with:\n          subject-name: ${{ steps.ecr.outputs.registry }}/clinic-agent\n          subject-digest: ${{ steps.build.outputs.digest }}\n          push-to-registry: true\nname: deploy\n\n# Deploys the image digest named in release/manifest.json. The digest reaches the manifest through\n# a reviewed release PR, so what runs is always a reviewed commit.\non:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      emergency:\n        description: Emergency change (hotfix/* branch, production-emergency environment)\n        type: boolean\n        default: false\n      owner:\n        description: Emergency only - person accountable for this change\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n      reason:\n        description: Emergency only - why this cannot wait for a normal release\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n      expires_on:\n        description: Emergency only - date (YYYY-MM-DD) by which it is replaced by a normal release\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n  id-token: write\n  issues: write\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: deploy-production\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    environment: ${{ inputs.emergency && 'production-emergency' || 'production' }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@08eba0b27e820071cde6df949e0beb9ba4906955 # v4.3.0\n\n      - name: Emergency change record is complete\n        if: inputs.emergency\n        env:\n          OWNER: ${{ inputs.owner }}\n          REASON: ${{ inputs.reason }}\n          EXPIRES_ON: ${{ inputs.expires_on }}\n        run: |\n          test -n \"$OWNER\" || { echo \"owner is required\"; exit 1; }\n          test -n \"$REASON\" || { echo \"reason is required\"; exit 1; }\n          date -d \"$EXPIRES_ON\" +%F >/dev/null || { echo \"expires_on must be a date\"; exit 1; }\n          [[ \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" == hotfix/* ]] || { echo \"emergency deploys come from hotfix/* branches\"; exit 1; }\n\n      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@a03048d87541d1d9fcf2ecf528a4a65ba9bd7838 # v5.0.0\n        with:\n          role-to-assume: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-deploy\n          aws-region: us-west-2\n\n      - uses: sigstore/cosign-installer@d58896d6a1865668819e1d91763c7751a165e159 # v3.9.2\n        with:\n          cosign-release: v2.6.2\n\n      - name: Verify image signature\n        run: |\n          DIGEST=$(jq -r .image.digest release/manifest.json)\n          REPO=$(jq -r .image.repository release/manifest.json)\n          cosign verify \"$REPO@$DIGEST\" \\\n            --certificate-identity \"https://github.com/northbay-clinics/clinic-agent/.github/workflows/ci.yml@refs/heads/main\" \\\n            --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\n          grep -q \"$DIGEST\" k8s/deployment.yaml || { echo \"k8s/deployment.yaml does not use the manifest digest\"; exit 1; }\n\n      - name: Apply\n        run: |\n          aws eks update-kubeconfig --name clinic-agent-prod\n          kubectl apply -f k8s/deployment.yaml\n          kubectl -n clinic-agent annotate deployment/clinic-agent --overwrite \\\n            northbay.example/git-sha=\"$GITHUB_SHA\" \\\n            northbay.example/release=\"$(jq -r .release release/manifest.json)\" \\\n            northbay.example/deployed-by=\"$GITHUB_ACTOR\" \\\n            northbay.example/run=\"$GITHUB_SERVER_URL/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$GITHUB_RUN_ID\"\n          kubectl -n clinic-agent rollout status deployment/clinic-agent --timeout=5m\n\n      - name: Open follow-up review for emergency change\n        if: inputs.emergency\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          OWNER: ${{ inputs.owner }}\n          REASON: ${{ inputs.reason }}\n          EXPIRES_ON: ${{ inputs.expires_on }}\n        run: |\n          gh issue create \\\n            --title \"Follow-up review: emergency deploy ${GITHUB_SHA::8}\" \\\n            --label emergency-change,needs-review \\\n            --assignee \"$OWNER\" \\\n            --body \"Owner: $OWNER\n          Reason: $REASON\n          Ends: $EXPIRES_ON\n          Commit: $GITHUB_SHA\n          Approved in environment production-emergency by a required reviewer (see run $GITHUB_RUN_ID).\n          Review and merge to main via normal PR before the end date.\"\n{\n  \"release\": \"clinic-agent-3.4.1\",\n  \"agentTypeId\": \"sha256:7c2e91f04ab35d6e8f1029c4b7a6d3e5f8091a2b3c4d5e6f708192a3b4c5d6e7\",\n  \"image\": {\n    \"repository\": \"418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent\",\n    \"digest\": \"sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\"\n  },\n  \"harness\": {\n    \"version\": \"3.4.1\",\n    \"gitSha\": \"e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\"\n  },\n  \"prompts\": [\n    { \"path\": \"prompts/system.md\", \"sha256\": \"5d1e0c9b8a7f6e5d4c3b2a1908f7e6d5c4b3a291807f6e5d4c3b2a19087f6e5d\" },\n    { \"path\": \"prompts/intent-classifier.txt\", \"sha256\": \"a3f9e1d7c5b3a1f9e7d5c3b1a9f7e5d3c1b9a7f5e3d1c9b7a5f3e1d9c7b5a3f1\" }\n  ],\n  \"models\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"agent\",\n      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n      \"requestedId\": \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\n      \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n      \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n      \"adapter\": null,\n      \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"intent_classifier\",\n      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n      \"requestedId\": \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\",\n      \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n      \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n      \"adapter\": null,\n      \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": {\n    \"allowlist\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\",\n    \"mcpServers\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"ehr\",\n        \"url\": \"https://ehr-mcp.internal.northbay-clinics.example/mcp\",\n        \"tlsCertSha256\": \"1f6a9c3e5b7d9f1a3c5e7b9d1f3a5c7e9b1d3f5a7c9e1b3d5f7a9c1e3b5d7f9a\",\n        \"owner\": \"ehr-integrations@northbay-clinics.example\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"native\": [\"payments\", \"sms\", \"insurance\"]\n  },\n  \"peers\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"eligibility-agent\",\n      \"url\": \"https://eligibility.partners.northbay-clinics.example/a2a\",\n      \"owner\": \"revenue-cycle@northbay-clinics.example\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"awsRole\": \"arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\",\n    \"ehrScopes\": [\"patient.read\", \"appointment.read\", \"appointment.write\"],\n    \"paymentsScopes\": [\"deposits.refund\"],\n    \"eligibilityScopes\": [\"eligibility:read\"]\n  },\n  \"memory\": \"none\",\n  \"retrieval\": \"none\",\n  \"network\": { \"policy\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml#clinic-agent-egress\", \"egressProxy\": \"egress-proxy.platform.svc:3128\" },\n  \"budgets\": \"config/budgets.yaml\",\n  \"policies\": { \"action\": \"config/policy.yaml\", \"actionPolicyVersion\": \"2026-09-18.3\" }\n}\n# clinic-agent\n\nPatient-scheduling agent for the Northbay Clinic Group. Patients reach it by SMS or by the web chat\nwidget on each clinic's site. It looks up, books, reschedules, and cancels appointments in the EHR,\nsends SMS reminders, refunds no-show deposits, and asks the insurance-eligibility agent whether a\nvisit is covered.\n\nEach clinic is a tenant. A clinic's patients, appointments, deposits, and EHR credentials are kept\nseparate from every other clinic's.\n\n## Components\n\n| Piece | Where | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n\nThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\nthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n\n## High-impact actions\n\n`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\nthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\nretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n\n```bash\naws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\\n  --item '{\"pk\":{\"S\":\"global\"},\"halted\":{\"BOOL\":true},\"by\":{\"S\":\"<you>\"}}'\n```\n\nRunning work checks the flag before each model turn and each tool call, and a watcher aborts in-flight\nrequests within 2 seconds.\n\n## Identity\n\n`src/agent/identity.ts` computes the agent-type-id from the image digest, harness version, prompts,\nmodel IDs, and config. Each pod also gets a random agent-instance-id at start. Both are on every\naudit record together with the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, and trace context.\n\n## Build and test\n\n```bash\nnpm ci\nnpm run lint\nnpm test\nnpm run build\n```\n\n## Release\n\nMerges to `main` need two reviews and a code owner review for prompts, config, infra, and manifests.\n`deploy.yml` builds, signs, and deploys by digest to the `production` environment, which has required\nreviewers. Emergency deploys use the same workflow with `emergency: true` and must name an owner,\na reason, and an end date; the workflow opens a follow-up review issue.\n\n## Owners\n\n- Accountable party: Northbay Clinic Group, Patient Access (VP Patient Access)\n- Operational owner: agent-platform team, `#agent-platform-oncall`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
