ontainer, or the sandbox call falls back to local execution on error. Answer yes if no such code runs.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== B12.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"B12.1\",\n  \"check\": \"The harness, system prompt, and rules files are in version control and loaded from the reviewed build, not fetched at run time from a database, URL, or feature flag.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find where the system prompt and rules are loaded (`system_prompt`, `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `prompts/`). 2) Check they come from files in the repo or build. 3) Answer no if any part is fetched at run time from a database, URL, feature flag, or env var with no recorded version, or a remote source overrides the file when available.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== B12.2\n{\n  \"id\": \"B12.2\",\n  \"check\": \"CODEOWNERS or required-review rules cover the prompt, rules, and harness files.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Read `CODEOWNERS` and review rules (`.github/`, rulesets, branch protection IaC). 2) Check patterns match prompt, rules, and harness paths. 3) Answer no if those paths are uncovered, the pattern misses them (wrong glob, case), or no CODEOWNERS exists. Answer unknown if required reviews are set only in repo settings outside the code.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== B12.3\n{\n  \"id\": \"B12.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Production deploys run only from CI on the reviewed branch and record the commit, tag, or digest deployed.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Read deploy workflows and scripts. 2) Check deploy triggers only on the reviewed branch and records commit, tag, or digest. 3) Answer no if `workflow_dispatch` or a script deploys any branch or local build, deploy scripts accept manual laptop pushes, or no version is recorded. Answer unknown if deploy is outside this repo.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== B12.4\n{\n  \"id\": \"B12.4\",\n  \"check\": \"Branch protection config blocks force-pushes and history rewrites on the source branch.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Search for branch protection IaC (`github_branch_protection`, rulesets JSON). 2) Check force-push and deletion are blocked on the source branch. 3) Answer no if `allow_force_pushes: true` or bypass is open to the agent's identity. Answer unknown if protection is set only in repo settings and not in code.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== R02.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"R02.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Outside content (API responses, tool output, documents, connector messages) goes into user or tool message roles, never into the system or policy prompt.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find where model requests are built (`system=`, `messages`, `role: system`, prompt templates). 2) Trace outside content (tool output, documents, API responses) into the request. 3) Answer no if any outside content is concatenated into the system or policy prompt, including retrieved context or tool descriptions from servers.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== R02.4\n{\n  \"id\": \"R02.4\",\n  \"check\": \"Containment does not rely on prompt wording, delimiters, or an injection detector.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find the defenses relied on for injection. 2) Check whether removing prompt wording, delimiters, or the detector would leave harmful actions blocked. 3) Answer no if containment depends on system-prompt rules, delimiter tags, or a detector, with no code-level block behind it.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n=== R03.3\n{\n  \"id\": \"R03.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Generated SQL uses parameterized queries, shell calls use argument lists with no string-built commands, and HTML output is escaped for its context.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Search for SQL, shell, and HTML built from generated output (`execute(f`, `+ query`, `shell=True`, `exec(`, `innerHTML`, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, `|safe`). 2) Check for parameters, argument lists, and context escaping. 3) Answer no if any query or command is string-built, uses `shell=True` or `sh -c` with model input, or HTML is unescaped.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n     1\timport { DynamoDBClient } from \"@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb\";\n     2\timport { DynamoDBDocumentClient, GetCommand, PutCommand } from \"@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb\";\n     3\timport { createHash, randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\n     4\timport { env, policy } from \"../config.js\";\n     5\t\n     6\t// Staff approvals for high-impact tools. The agent creates a pending request; a front-desk lead or\n     7\t// clinic manager approves it in the staff console (which writes status, approvedBy, approverRole,\n     8\t// approvedAt); the agent then retries the tool with the approval id.\n     9\t\n    10\texport interface ApprovalRecord {\n    11\t  id: string;\n    12\t  status: \"pending\" | \"approved\" | \"rejected\";\n    13\t  tool: string;\n    14\t  tenantId: string;\n    15\t  agentInstanceId: string;\n    16\t  runId: string;\n    17\t  argsHash: string;\n    18\t  summary: string;\n    19\t  requestedAt: string;\n    20\t  expiresAt: string;\n    21\t  approvedBy?: string;\n    22\t  approverRole?: string;\n    23\t  approvedAt?: string;\n    24\t}\n    25\t\n    26\tconst ddb = DynamoDBDocumentClient.from(new DynamoDBClient({ region: env.region }));\n    27\t\n    28\texport function hashArgs(args: Record<string, unknown>): string {\n    29\t  const canonical = JSON.stringify(args, Object.keys(args).sort());\n    30\t  return createHash(\"sha256\").update(canonical).digest(\"hex\");\n    31\t}\n    32\t\n    33\texport async function requestApproval(req: {\n    34\t  tool: string;\n    35\t  tenantId: string;\n    36\t  agentInstanceId: string;\n    37\t  runId: string;\n    38\t  args: Record<string, unknown>;\n    39\t  summary: string;\n    40\t}): Promise<ApprovalRecord> {\n    41\t  const now = Date.now();\n    42\t  const rec: ApprovalRecord = {\n    43\t    id: randomUUID(),\n    44\t    status: \"pending\",\n    45\t    tool: req.tool,\n    46\t    tenantId: req.tenantId,\n    47\t    agentInstanceId: req.agentInstanceId,\n    48\t    runId: req.runId,\n    49\t    argsHash: hashArgs(req.args),\n    50\t    summary: req.summary,\n    51\t    requestedAt: new Date(now).toISOString(),\n    52\t    expiresAt: new Date(now + policy.approval.ttlSeconds * 1000).toISOString(),\n    53\t  };\n    54\t  await ddb.send(new PutCommand({ TableName: policy.approval.table, Item: rec, ConditionExpression: \"attribute_not_exists(id)\" }));\n    55\t  return rec;\n    56\t}\n    57\t\n    58\texport type ApprovalCheck = { ok: true; approval: ApprovalRecord } | { ok: false; reason: string };\n    59\t\n    60\texport async function checkApproval(req: {\n    61\t  approvalId: string;\n    62\t  tool: string;\n    63\t  tenantId: string;\n    64\t  args: Record<string, unknown>;\n    65\t}): Promise<ApprovalCheck> {\n    66\t  let rec: ApprovalRecord | undefined;\n    67\t  try {\n    68\t    const res = await ddb.send(new GetCommand({ TableName: policy.approval.table, Key: { id: req.approvalId }, ConsistentRead: true }));\n    69\t    rec = res.Item as ApprovalRecord | undefined;\n    70\t  } catch (err) {\n    71\t    return { ok: false, reason: `approval store unavailable: ${(err as Error).message}` };\n    72\t  }\n    73\t  if (!rec) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval not found\" };\n    74\t  if (rec.status !== \"approved\") return { ok: false, reason: `approval is ${rec.status}` };\n    75\t  if (rec.tool !== req.tool) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval is for a different tool\" };\n    76\t  if (rec.tenantId !== req.tenantId) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval is for a different clinic\" };\n    77\t  if (Date.parse(rec.expiresAt) <= Date.now()) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval expired\" };\n    78\t  if (!rec.approverRole || !policy.approval.approverRoles.includes(rec.approverRole)) {\n    79\t    return { ok: false, reason: \"approver lacks authority\" };\n    80\t  }\n    81\t  return { ok: true, approval: rec };\n    82\t}\n     1\t# Every tool the scheduling agent may call, with the task it serves.\n     2\t# The executor denies any tool not listed here. Annotations from servers (readOnlyHint and so on)\n     3\t# are not used for allow or approval decisions.\n     4\trole: scheduling_agent\n     5\ttools:\n     6\t  - tool: ehr__find_patient\n     7\t    reason: Match the sender to a patient record by date of birth and phone or email.\n     8\t  - tool: ehr__search_slots\n     9\t    reason: List open slots for a provider, location, and visit type.\n    10\t  - tool: ehr__get_appointment\n    11\t    reason: Read one appointment the patient asks about.\n    12\t  - tool: ehr__list_patient_appointments\n    13\t    reason: Show the patient their upcoming appointments.\n    14\t  - tool: ehr__book_appointment\n    15\t    reason: Book a slot the patient chose.\n    16\t  - tool: ehr__update_appointment\n    17\t    reason: Change time, provider, or status (confirmed / checked_in / no_show / cancelled) of an appointment.\n    18\t  - tool: ehr__cancel_appointment\n    19\t    reason: Cancel an appointment at the patient's request.\n    20\t  - tool: payments__refund_deposit\n    21\t    reason: Refund a no-show deposit after staff review.\n    22\t  - tool: sms__send_to_patient\n    23\t    reason: Send a templated message to the phone number on the patient's record.\n    24\t  - tool: sms__send_freeform\n    25\t    reason: Send a staff-approved message that is not one of the templates.\n    26\t  - tool: insurance__check_eligibility\n    27\t    reason: Ask the eligibility agent whether a visit is covered.\n28\nIf7878f59fe tool_registration src/agent/budget.ts:165\nI11c134ddd9 model_call src/agent/classifier.ts:45\nI1ae2dd3bba audit_write src/agent/loop.ts:107\nIf45cb9d300 handoff src/agent/loop.ts:111\nIf194378c0f handoff src/agent/loop.ts:20\nIff7ceb0cf2 audit_write s